  "answer": "**Final status: passing.** In the second verification run, all three configured stages passed: build, unit and component (run `20261021T141700Z-0f60dc`). It took one fix.\n\n**What failed:** On the first run, the unit stage failed with exit code 2 and the component stage was skipped. The failing test was `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`, which failed once for each target framework.\n\n**Root cause:** When the actual response has a field that the expected response doesn't, the diff output is meant to show `<absent>` in the \"expected\" slot. `DeltaFormatter` was printing `<not present>` instead, so the test's check for `<absent>` failed. The fixer judged the test to be right and the production code wrong, because `SemanticMatcher.cs` already uses the word \"absent\" for the same idea.\n\n**What changed:** One line in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`:\n```diff\n- expected = TestColor.Subtle(\"<not present>\");\n+ expected = TestColor.Subtle(\"<absent>\");\n```\n\nNothing was committed. The stages that ran are only the ones configured in `.lattice/verification.yaml`: build, unit and component. The integration tests and the skills checks were not run.",
